cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "hw-verify: a unified front end for the hw-verify hardware security toolkit"
message: "If you use this in academic work, please cite it."
type: software
authors:
  - alias: nickharris808
    website: "https://github.com/nickharris808"
repository-code: "https://github.com/nickharris808/hw-verify"
url: "https://huggingface.co/spaces/nickh007/hw-verify"
abstract: >-
  One install and one command over three checkers: constant-time RTL, first-order masking, and bounds-check patch completeness. Delegates to each tool's own CLI so there is a single implementation of every flag, and passes exit codes through unchanged -- including the third code that distinguishes 'no verdict was reached' from 'leaky'.
keywords:
  - hardware security
  - constant-time
  - side-channel
  - formal verification
  - cli
license: Apache-2.0
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-07-28"
